{"id":"20260827T024051.262134924Z-ddaafaf4","time":"2026-08-27T02:40:51.262134924Z","session_id":"session-20260827T023925.143803041Z","task_id":"task-1787798365144236629","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  semaphore.Weighted.TryAcquire and Acquire duplicate the decision about whether a request can proceed immediately. Factor that decision into one place so the two paths cannot diverge, with no change to observable behaviour.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Acquire and TryAcquire currently duplicate the predicate s.size-s.cur \u003e= n \u0026\u0026 s.waiters.Len() == 0 and increment s.cur by n when it succeeds. (semaphore/semaphore.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Acquire checks context cancellation before attempting immediate acquisition and retains separate oversized-request and queued-waiter paths. (semaphore.Weighted.Acquire) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Both public acquisition methods reject negative weights before entering their acquisition logic. (semaphore.Weighted) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Existing semaphore tests cover basic immediate success and failure for both methods, negative-weight panics, cancellation, and waiter fairness. (semaphore/semaphore_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped Sensei preflight classifies this single-file change as LOW_RISK with sufficient indexed-file coverage, no anchored governing rule, and no required tests or forbidden fixes. (semaphore/semaphore.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei identifies semaphore.Weighted and a candidate public API contract for this file, but verifies no directly governing invariants. (semaphore/semaphore.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei task_briefing returned the