{"id":"20260827T024051.262243905Z-1ea095ad","time":"2026-08-27T02:40:51.262243905Z","session_id":"session-20260827T023925.143803041Z","task_id":"task-1787798365144236629","source":"architect","kind":"plan.proposed","summary":"Centralize Weighted's immediate-acquisition decision and state update without changing semaphore behavior.\n\nPlan:\n  1. Add an unexported helper that, while s.mu is held, checks available capacity and the absence of queued waiters, increments s.cur on success, and returns the decision.\n  2. Replace Acquire's inline immediate-acquisition predicate and state update with the helper after its existing context-cancellation check.\n  3. Replace TryAcquire's duplicated predicate and state update with the same helper while preserving its negative-weight validation and mutex boundary.\n  4. Run the semaphore package tests to verify acquisition, cancellation, fairness, and panic behavior remain unchanged.","payload":{"decision":"proceed","summary":"Centralize Weighted's immediate-acquisition decision and state update without changing semaphore behavior.","steps":["Add an unexported helper that, while s.mu is held, checks available capacity and the absence of queued waiters, increments s.cur on success, and returns the decision.","Replace Acquire's inline immediate-acquisition predicate and state update with the helper after its existing context-cancellation check.","Replace TryAcquire's duplicated predicate and state update with the same helper while preserving its negative-weight validation and mutex boundary.","Run the semaphore package tests to verify acquisition, cancellation, fairness, and panic behavior remain unchanged."],"consequences":"The public API and observable behavior remain unchanged; Acquire and TryAcquire can no longer diverge in their immediate-acquisition capacity, queue-fairness, or state-update logic.","files":["semaphore/semaphore.go"],"mode":"modify","plan":"Introduce one lock-protected internal helper that decides whether a weighted request may proceed immediately and records a successful acquisition. Route both Acquire and TryAcquire through it while preserving validation, cancellation ordering, locking, fairness, and blocking behavior.","claims":[{"statement":"Acquire and TryAcquire currently duplicate the predicate s.size-s.cur \u003e= n \u0026\u0026 s.waiters.Len() == 0 and increment s.cur by n when it succeeds.","about":"semaphore/semaphore.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Acquire checks context cancellation before attempting immediate acquisition and retains separate oversized-request and queued-waiter paths.","about":"semaphore.Weighted.Acquire","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Both public acquisition methods reject negative weights before entering their acquisition logic.","about":"semaphore.Weighted","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Existing semaphore tests cover basic immediate success and failure for both methods, negative-weight panics, cancellation, and waiter fairness.","about":"semaphore/semaphore_test.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Scoped Sensei preflight classifies this single-file change as LOW_RISK with sufficient indexed-file coverage, no anchored governing rule, and no required tests or forbidden fixes.","about":"semaphore/semaphore.go","source":"graph"},{"statement":"Sensei identifies semaphore.Weighted and a candidate public API contract for this file, but verifies no directly governing invariants.","about":"semaphore/semaphore.go","source":"graph"},{"statement":"Sensei task_briefing returned the exact error: Mcp error: -32000: no task session exists in this repository.","about":"task-scoped guidance for semaphore/semaphore.go","source":"graph"}]}}
